  "question": {
    "text": "If <math><mn>0.1</mn><mi>&nbsp;J</mi></math> of energy is stored for the flow of the current of <math><mn>0.2</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>A</mn></math> in an inductor, then its inductance value (in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>) is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "The energy stored in an inductor is given by the formula<br /><br /><math><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>L</mi><msup><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />Given, <math><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mi>&nbsp;J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>A</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mn>0.1</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>L</mi><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0.2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0.2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>H</mn></math>"
  }
}